/* book exam traps: Sign of N: use H = h − N, never H = h + N. With N = −82.0 m and h = 52.3 m the wrong formula gives H = −29.7 m, a point below mean sea level, while the correct one gives H = 134.3 m. A negative N increases H. | Ellipsoidal height h and orthometric height H are not the same. h comes from GNSS; H is the height above the geoid. | Latitude and longitude need a horizontal datum; a height needs a vertical datum. A coordinate pair alone does not fix a height. | UTM easting and northing are meaningless without the zone and hemisphere. | When mixing coordinates from two datums, transform first. Do not average raw coordinates from WGS84 and a local datum. */
